# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three point at the ryp-core Neon project. Connect as the NOBYPASSRLS roles, never as
# neondb_owner — the owner would satisfy every policy and RLS would silently stop meaning anything.

# atlas_app over the POOLER host (contains ".pooler."). eco's withRls sets its session vars
# transaction-locally, which is what makes the pooler safe here.
DATABASE_URL=
# Same role, DIRECT host. For drizzle migrations and any session-scoped work — PgBouncer runs in
# transaction mode and drops session state.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
# billing_svc — the only role that may write entitlements, plans, and users.plan. Used by the seed
# script and (later) the Stripe webhook. Never by a user-facing route.
BILLING_DATABASE_URL=

# FORGE's two principals. Both NOBYPASSRLS, NOINHERIT; neither is atlas_app. If either is unset, names the
# wrong role, or equals another credential here, server/index.ts does NOT mount /api/forge (it answers 503
# and says so at boot) — there is no fallback to atlas_app, which would hand a player the coach's grants.
# forge_app — the request path: every player read and write on the FORGE tables.
FORGE_APP_DATABASE_URL=
# forge_svc — the service principal and the ONLY one that may stamp a ladder rung or an assignment
# completion. Used by POST /api/forge/sessions/:id/complete and nowhere else. Never in a request path.
FORGE_SVC_DATABASE_URL=

# ─── Slack feedback (Testing) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A feedback button on Luke's served pages posts the note + a screenshot to a Slack channel, one thread
# per tester per day. If EITHER is unset or malformed, /api/feedback answers 503, no button is injected,
# and boot logs which variable (by name only).
# A BOT token (xoxb-…), NOT an incoming webhook — a webhook cannot upload a file. Scopes:
#   files:write, chat:write, and channels:history (groups:history for a private channel — the
#   thread lookup needs it; without it everything still posts, just never threaded).
# INVITE THE BOT to the channel, or every call answers not_in_channel.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# The channel ID (C… or G…; Slack: channel name → About → bottom of the dialog). NOT "#name".
SLACK_FEEDBACK_CHANNEL=

# The API port. Not 5000: Red and Locker Room both take it and all three get run at once.
# vite.config.ts reads this to aim its /api dev proxy, so changing it here is enough.
PORT=5055

# ─── Firebase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Project rypstick-ios, shared with Red and Locker Room ON PURPOSE. firebase_uid is the join key
# into public.users, so a separate project would give the same person a different identity per app
# and break every cross-app read. Do not point Atlas at a new project.
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=rypstick-ios
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=       # PEM, \n-escaped, double-quoted. Never a VITE_ var — VITE_ vars ship to the browser.

# Client-safe Firebase config (public by design; these identify the project, they don't authorize).
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=rypstick-ios
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=rypstick-ios.firebaseapp.com

# ── FEEDBACK → SLACK ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A bot token, NOT an incoming webhook: webhooks cannot upload files.
# Scopes: files:write, chat:write, and channels:history (groups:history for a private channel).
# Without the history scope everything posts but threading silently never happens.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# The channel ID (C… or G…), not a #name. Use a PRIVATE channel: screenshots of a coach's screen
# carry a student's name, notes and intake answers, and some students are minors.
SLACK_FEEDBACK_CHANNEL=
# ⚠️ REQUIRED. Comma-separated emails. The button is injected ONLY for these people and the route
# refuses everyone else. Empty = the feature stays off, which is the safe default.
SLACK_FEEDBACK_TESTERS=
